<title>NORWAY: Aker Maritime 1996 profits rise.</title>
<headline>Aker Maritime 1996 profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31.</p>
<p>				 (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>  Operating income	     10,825	vs	8,131</p>
<p>  Operating result		  230	vs	  188</p>
<p>  Result after financials	 301	vs	  177</p>
<p>  Net profit			  229	vs	   90</p>
<p>Dividend  1.60 crowns per share NOTE - Full name of Norwegian offshore services company is Aker Maritime ASA. The company was formed last November after Aker ASA spun off its Oil and Gas Technology division and merged it with offshore supplier Maritime Group.</p>
<p>A Reuter poll of nine analysts forecast an operating result of 298 million crowns and pre-tax profits of 290 million crowns. Three analysts recommended to buy the share, one said hold, four said sell and one declined to give a view.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
